---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="Itto-ryu Tech is an open-source collection of rule-based TradingView indicators.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 pt-14 space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold">About</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Itto-ryu (一刀流)</strong> means "the school of one sword". The name is a reminder that good trading
      starts from a simple system you can test and practise until it becomes habit, not from stacking as many
      indicators as possible.
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold pt-4">What is different here</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3">
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-shu">—</span><span><strong>Failed results are published.</strong> If a signal shows no edge in testing, we say so.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-shu">—</span><span><strong>Everything is open-source.</strong> The Pine Script indicators and this website's code are public.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-shu">—</span><span><strong>Built for practice.</strong> This project is where the author trains their own skills in public.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold pt-4">Author</h2>
    <p>
      A TFEX / SET50 trader who builds the [Itto-Ryu] indicator family on TradingView.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted">
      Feedback and ideas:
      <a href="https://github.com/Thiranat18/itto-ryu-dojo/issues" class="underline hover:text-paper">GitHub Issues</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
